metadata.description:
The uploaded data comprises three primary folders titled: THz-TDS, Raman data, and XRD data

THz-TDS
This folder has four subfolders, each contains terahertz time-domain transmission data. In every data file, the first column represents the time delay, and the second column corresponds to the transmitted electric field (e-field). 
The measurements are named in the format: "LnpmXYi_11h_1", where:
 n = 1 for GST225, 3 for GST326;
m =1 for as-grown, 2 for sample annealed at 155 C, 3 at 205 C,  4 at 255 C,  5 at 305 C, 6 at 355 C, and 7 at 405 C;
X = Z indicates sapphire substrate and without X is silicon substrate;
Y = M for thin-film+substrate, S for bare substrate only, R for reference;
i = 1, 2 or 3 indicates measurement spots 1, 2 and 3 respectively. 
In cases where the file name is prefixed by 'replica', for example replicaLnpmXYi_11h_1, it refers to newly fabricated samples measured under the same conditions.  


Raman data
Raman measurements are named in the format: "Ln_i_laser 785nm_F25_r50_250_ob10_g600_t2s_ac20_spotj", where:
n = 2 for GST225, 3 for GST326;
i = 1 to 7, representing the as-grown state and annealed samples at 155 C, 205 C, 255 C, 305 C, 355 C and 405 C, respectively;
j = 1 to 3, indicating the three different measurement spots per sample.
Each Raman dataset contains two columns: the first column is the Raman shift, and second column is the corresponding intensity.  

XRD data
XRD files are named in the format: "Ln.i_exported", where:
n = 2 for GST225, 3 for GST326;
i = 1 to 7, corresponding to the as-grown sample and annealed samples at 155 C, 205 C, 255 C, 305 C, 355 C and 405 C, respectively.
Each XRD file contains two columns: the first column is the diffraction angle (2 theta), and the second column is the intensity.
